essentially if you would like to implement a RAM like our fmodel / asim RAMs ...

--> you could either create a file and mmap share it between processes (different simulators)

--> or have a common file path in mind but fallocate upfront and then mmap and use

With the former you pay for memory only when you actually read/write but on the first
read you access disk because it doesnt know that your file contents are zero.

also you ll have to create the file upfront


With the latter you dont have to create the file. you can fallocate. after which 
first reads dont touch disk the kernel takes care of that. Thanks to Peter Zilkstra
for pointing that out.

